From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:14:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: Answer DV_E_CLIPFORMAT for data of no format the cache
 does not have.

A view cache entry, added for any format, takes the format of the
first presentation put into it; asking for data with no format after
that finds no entry, and the cache answered OLE_E_BLANK as for a format
it does not hold.  ole32's tests expect DV_E_CLIPFORMAT from Windows,
while a view cache that is still blank answers OLE_E_BLANK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ole32/datacache.c b/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
index be0d6788892..43a30894e79 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/datacache.c
@@ -1525,9 +1525,10 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI DataCache_GetData(
 
     memset(pmedium, 0, sizeof(*pmedium));
 
+    /* no format at all is only something to ask a view cache that is still blank for */
     cache_entry = DataCache_GetEntryForFormatEtc(This, pformatetcIn);
     if (!cache_entry)
-        return OLE_E_BLANK;
+        return pformatetcIn->cfFormat ? OLE_E_BLANK : DV_E_CLIPFORMAT;
 
     return DataCacheEntry_GetData(cache_entry, This->presentationStorage, pformatetcIn, pmedium);
 }
diff --git a/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c b/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
index 25ad58b6349..4a844cf59fb 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
+++ b/dlls/ole32/tests/ole2.c
@@ -2689,7 +2689,7 @@ static void test_data_cache_updatecache( void )
     hr = IDataObject_GetData(data, &emf_fmt, &medium);
     ok(hr == OLE_E_BLANK, "Got hr %#lx.\n", hr);
     hr = IDataObject_GetData(data, &view_fmt, &medium);
-    todo_wine ok(hr == DV_E_CLIPFORMAT, "Got hr %#lx.\n", hr);
+    ok(hr == DV_E_CLIPFORMAT, "Got hr %#lx.\n", hr);
 
     data_object_format = &emf_fmt;
     hr = IOleCache2_UpdateCache( cache, &DataObject, UPDFCACHE_ALL, NULL );
